---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import features from "../data/features.json";
---
<SiteLayout title="Retail POS Mobile — Android-first POS in development" description="Retail POS Mobile is being built as an independent, offline-first retail POS for small shops. Public download is not available yet." path="/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> In foundation development</span>
      <h1>A retail POS built for the realities of the <span>shop floor.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Retail POS Mobile is being developed as an Android-first product for everyday retail work—designed around clear counter flows, traceable stock, and honest offline behavior.</p>
      <div class="status-line"><span class="status-pill status-foundation"><span class="status-dot"></span> Pre-launch</span><span class="status-pill status-unavailable"><span class="status-dot"></span> Public download unavailable</span></div>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/product/">Explore the product direction <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">Check release status</a></div>
      <p class="hero-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 20 6v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-8 10-4.5-1.5-8-5-8-10V6l8-3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/><path d="m8.5 12 2.2 2.2 4.8-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> We will publish a download only after a signed build passes its release checks.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-panel" aria-label="Current development status">
      <div class="panel-topline"><span class="panel-label">Development snapshot</span><span class="panel-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M7 3.5h7l4 4V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H7a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4.5a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M14 3.5V8h4M9 12h6M9 16h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span></div>
      <h2 class="panel-title">Built carefully, released honestly.</h2><p class="panel-subtitle">The mobile repository is establishing its production foundation before operational workflows are released.</p>
      <div class="snapshot-list"><div class="snapshot-row"><span>Primary platform</span><strong>Android first</strong></div><div class="snapshot-row"><span>Development stage</span><strong>Foundation work</strong></div><div class="snapshot-row"><span>Public APK</span><strong>Not available yet</strong></div><div class="snapshot-row"><span>Pricing / pilot</span><strong>Not announced</strong></div></div>
      <div class="panel-foot">This is a project-status summary, not a screenshot of a released app. Planned capabilities are described separately from current availability.</div>
    </aside>
  </div></section>
  <div class="trust-strip"><div class="container trust-strip-inner"><p><strong>Designed with the small-shop context in mind.</strong> Public claims stay tied to verified implementation.</p><div class="trust-items"><span>Android-first</span><span>PKR context</span><span>Offline-first goal</span><span>No public APK yet</span></div></div></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Product direction</span><h2>Everyday retail work, made easier to follow.</h2><p>The following areas describe the intended product—not features available in a public build today.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/features/">See the planned scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="card-grid">{features.map((feature,index)=><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned</span><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.outcome}</p><a class="text-link" href={feature.id==="offline"?"/offline-first/":"/features/"}>Explore scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section section-soft"><div class="container split-panel">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Offline, without pretending</span><h2>Disconnected devices cannot know what each other just sold.</h2><p>The intended design is to queue local work safely, retry without duplicating transactions, and surface conflicts for review instead of silently rewriting sales history.</p><p>This behavior is a design target and must be implemented and tested before it is advertised as available.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="/offline-first/">Read the offline approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="architecture-card"><span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned architecture</span><h3 style="margin-top:18px">A clear path for local work and sync</h3><p>Three boundaries keep the design understandable.</p><div class="flow-stack"><div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">01</span><div><strong>On-device data</strong><small>Fast local access for supported workflows</small></div></div><div class="flow-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">02</span><div><strong>Durable outbox</strong><small>Queue operations for safe retry and reconciliation</small></div></div><div class="flow-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">03</span><div><strong>Independent cloud backend</strong><small>Validate and reconcile when connectivity returns</small></div></div></div><p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:.8rem">Conceptual architecture only; not a claim that these workflows are released.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><h2>Want to know when a real build is ready?</h2><p>The download page will show the exact version, build, Android requirements, checksum, and release notes once an approved signed APK exists.</p></div><a class="button" href="/download/">View release status <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
